From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0047] reserve 4 GB and the guard per hardware bounds memory

Hardware bounds builds reserved 8 GB for every memory, the interpreter's
included. A memory now reserves 4 GB and the guard only when its module's code
skips bounds checks, and every other memory maps, grows and unmaps as in a
software bounds build. Reservations stop while the process still has room:
at a cap of half the address space by default, which the host can change, and
2 GB short of an address space limit. A reservation maps directly, without
os_mmap's retries and message, and after one finds no address space the next
waits until a memory has gone. A refused reservation fails the instantiate
with an error that says so, for the host to fall back on code that checks.
The signal handler turns a fault into a trap only inside a memory with the
reservation.

